Spoilers:

I hate playing wizards.  When I asked the game to give me a random character,
of course it gave me a wizard.  Disgusted, I saw a wand of digging in his
inventory and zapped it straight down.  Lo and behold, I landed in an
armor shop.  Having two scrolls of destroy armor, I figured what the heck,
I'll try on some armor.  A pair of speed boots and a cloak of invisibility
later, I saw this game had potential!  I threw a potion of paralysis at the
shopkeeper, zapped digging straight down, and ran like hell.  The next shop 
I encountered was also an armor shop, and from that I got gauntlets of power!

Things went fairly well after I found two scrolls of enchant weapon and
a potion of holy water and a dwarvish mithril coat.  A +4 athame is useful
against dwarves.  On the shop level there was even an uncursed magic lamp.
Unfortunately the altar was not of my alignment.  Amusingly, I stepped on
a polymorph trap while wearing my cloak of invisibility, and I turned into
a seventh level wizard with 16 str and 18 co, adding 3 and 5 points 
respectively to each of those abilities.  How lucky.

Later in the game I had occasion to go back to the second level and ran
into the shopkeeper, who nearly offed me, but I zapped sleep at him and
killed him.  On the first level I discovered an altar.  I blessed the
magic lamp, and got gray dragon scale mail therefrom.  A few levels later
a potion of gain energy turned out to have a friendly djinni, and I got
a shield of reflection.

The first level altar yielded first Magicbane, then Dragonbane, and then
stopped giving me anything for a long, long time.  Not having a very good
weapon, I was loath to try either the quest or Ludios, and got as far as
level 20 before discovering a shrine of my alignment.  While making holy
water, I became the Envoy of Balance, and Vorpal Blade in hand, the Dark
One and Ludios fell before me.  With forty thousand gold pieces in hand,
I lowered my armor class respectably, but then I forgot that after your
deity gives you a weapon, you cannot pray to him again for several hundred
turns.  Presto, my armor class was only -12!  Things looked grim until
I was able to scrounge up a magic marker from somewhere and wrote genocide
and enchant armor.  With liches genocided, I could take on Medusa and the
Castle safely.

The wand of wishing went for an attempted Yendorian Express Card (no luck--
there were already about seven artifacts in my game), a scroll of charging
(since my first magic marker had already run out, I charged it, wrote
charging, charged the wand, and had three more wishes), a helm of brilliance,
a ring of conflict, a magic marker, and a bag of holding.  While polypiling
gems I was amused to see 66 gray stones.  Not going to pick that up!

I refreshed a spellbook of magic mapping (my other one was untouched) and
proceeded to map out Hell.  Juiblex swallowed me, but did no damage while
I cut him up from inside.  I killed the Wizard, went to the vibrating
square, and retrieved the amulet, using conflict the entire way.  I zapped
one of my six wands of death at the High Priest of Moloch.

On the way back up, I threw a paralysis potion at the Wiz and ditched him
in Hell.  Very, very handy.

The Elemental Plane of Earth was no problem, but on the Plane of Air,
I encountered severe difficulties as five Archons and three Archon-summoning
titans ganged up on me.  I could wear any two of conflict, searching, and
levitation, but not all three.  I nearly died once as I took off searching and
put on conflict (20 hp), but Vorpy dispatched two Archons before my sole amulet
of life-saving was used up (being swallowed by air elementals really did
a lot of damage!); my ring of conflict handled the other summoned monsters
easily.  My ring of levitation blew up after I was struck by lightning, but
I had a spare in my bag.  Five times the Archons managed to lower me to fifty
hp (out of 200--I had never managed to get the Bell cursed), but each time I 
ran away.  With amazing luck and perseverance (I must have spent a thousand 
turns on that plane) I reduced them to one last Archon.  When it was two 
squares away, I moved to attack it and miraculously stepped on the portal.

A quite similar thing happened on the fire plane, except I didn't die.
My crystal ball had refused to recharge for the last five thousand turns
or so, and I was getting quite frustrated, but luckily I stepped on the
portal.

I floated about the water plane for a while and while flailing at some eels
I accidentally found the portal yet again, but wearing conflict.

Fortunately the Angels on the Astral Plane dispatched Death before he could
meet me, and I guessed the correct altar on the first try.

HP: 190(218) PW: 138(138) AC:-28 XP:25/50072303 S:1972564 (final score 4427628)
St:25 Dx:18 Co:17 (should have been 18) In:23 Wi:23 Ch:12

I had 98 sapphires, 18 dilithium crystals, 22 emeralds, and assorted other
diamonds and rubies and junk.  All in all, the luckiest game I have ever
played, especially on the Plane of Air.
 
This was the first time I had ever ascended on a non-PC system despite five 
years of playing hack.
